f0-4c30-ad58-838bb573d140" class="r-7ed71j alchemy-rte"><span style="width:100%"><h5>The Menstruation Phase</h5></span></div><div data-rid="b770f77c-c83b-43d7-9102-463bbb0c74cf" class="r-lkmndf alchemy-rte" style="--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-color:#2A2A2A;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-fontsize:14px;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-textdecoration:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-fontfamily:Quicksand;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-fontweight:400;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-lineheight:125%;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-textshadow:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-textstroke:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-letterspacing:0px;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-texttransform:undefined"><span style="width:100%"><p><strong>What happens?</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Hormone levels, including estrogen and progesterone, drop significantly, triggering the shedding of the uterine lining. This drop signals the release of prostaglandins, which cause the uterus to contract and shed its lining, resulting in cramps and inflammation. If you don’t have a condition like PCOS or endometriosis, studies indicate that the difference between someone with debilitating cramps and someone who barely notices theirs  comes down to prostaglandin levels.</p></span></div><div data-rid="d348a2ac-9450-47fb-8b49-dcede07b61ae" class="r-1skxvlv alchemy-rte" style="--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-color:#2A2A2A;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-fontsize:14px;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-textdecoration:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-fontfamily:Quicksand;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-lineheight:125%;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-textshadow:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-textstroke:undefined;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-letterspacing:0px;--replo-library-7229a9be-0ff2-4194-85c2-a9c88cbfa244-styles-9f4e2106-1742-4edd-a195-a474795b8511-attributes-texttransform:undefined"><span style="width:100%"><p><strong>How monthlies helps:<br></strong><br></p><p>Formulated with potent anti-inflammatory ingredients like <strong>Ginger Root Extract, Turmeric, and Aniseed</strong>, monthlies targets inflammation and helps reduce uterine contractions. <strong>Magnesium</strong> supports muscle relaxation and reduces tension, while <strong>Vitamin B Complex</strong> aids in energy production and mood stabilization. The unique blend works to calm pain amplifiers at their source, helping ease cramps without the side effects associated with traditional painkillers.</p></span></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-state="inactive" data-orientation="vertical" role="tabpanel" aria-labell